Sec. 3.
Minnesota Statutes 2024, section 638.14, subdivision 5, is amended to read:

Subd. 5.
Applicant appearance; third-party statements.
(a) Except as provided for in paragraph (e), an applicant for clemency must appear before the commission either in person or through available forms of telecommunication.
(b) The victim of an applicant's crime may appear and speak at the meeting or submit a written statement to the commission. The commission may treat a victim's written statement as confidential and not disclose the statement to the applicant or the public if there is or has been an order for protection, harassment restraining order, or other no-contact order prohibiting the applicant from contacting the victim. At the request of the victim, the commission may treat a victim's written statement as confidential and not disclose the statement to the public.
